---
// Figure: a second delete after a delay catches the racing fills that land before it.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Slider from '../shared/Slider.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './invalidation.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="inv-double" title="Deleting again after a delay" controls="none"
  caption="Illustrative model of 4,000 racing fills: most fills take tens of milliseconds, and one in fifty is held up for between 0.2 and 6 seconds. With the primary, a fill races only if it is in progress when the write commits, which slow fills are far more likely to be. With the replica, the reader misses after the delete (reads arrive about twice a second) and reads a replica 500 ms behind. The last bar counts every old value stored 3 seconds or more after the first delete. The vertical axis is square-root scaled so the small bars stay visible; this makes the bars far from zero look larger than their share, so read the shares from the counters.">
  <Fragment slot="params">
    <Slider name="delay" label="Second delete after" min={0} max={3000} step={50} value={500} unit="ms" />
    <Choice name="source" label="Readers read from" value="primary"
      options={[{ value: 'primary', label: 'the primary' }, { value: 'replica', label: 'a replica 500 ms behind' }]} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="caught" label="Old values removed" value="–" kind="write" />
    <Readout name="missed" label="Old values left until expiry" value="–" kind="stale" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>The bars show when racing fills store their old value, counted from the writer's first delete. Bars left of the marker land before the second delete and are removed by it; bars to the right land after it and stay until they expire.</p>
    <p>Reading from the primary, a second delete after 50 ms removes about 40% of the old values, after 500 ms about 60%, and after 2 seconds about 80%. Most racing fills are slow ones, because a fill has to be in progress when the write commits, and a slow fill is in progress for longer. Reading from a replica 500 ms behind, about two writes in three produce an old value in this model, where the key is read twice a second, and almost every old value lands within the first 600 ms or so, so a 500 ms delay removes about 95%, but a 100 ms delay only about 20%. No delay removes them all, because there is no upper limit on how long a fill can be held up.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { histogram } from '../shared/chart.mjs';
  import { racingSetTimes, caughtShare } from './double-delete-model.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="inv-double"]').forEach(root => {
    const chart = histogram(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Histogram of when racing fills store an old value, after the first delete, split by whether the second delete removes them',
      height: 240,
      bins: { min: 0, max: 3000, count: 60 },
      series: [{ id: 'caught', label: 'Removed by the second delete', kind: 'write' }, { id: 'missed', label: 'Lands after it, stays stale', kind: 'stale' }],
      x: { label: 'Time after the first delete', format: (v: number) => (v >= 1000 ? `${v / 1000} s` : v ? `${v} ms` : `0`) },
      y: { label: 'Old values stored (square-root scale)', scale: 'sqrt' },
    });
    const cache: Record<string, number[]> = {};
    const times = (source: string) => (cache[source] ??= racingSetTimes({ source, lag: 500 }));
    bindParams(root, (params: any) => {
      const t = times(params.source);
      const d = params.delay;
      chart.set({ caught: t.filter(v => v < d), missed: t.filter(v => v >= d) });
      chart.mark('delay', d, `second delete, ${d >= 1000 ? `${d / 1000} s` : `${d} ms`}`);
      const c = caughtShare(t, d);
      setReadouts(root, { caught: `${Math.round(c * 100)}%`, missed: `${Math.round((1 - c) * 100)}%` });
    });
  });
</script>
